# Release gate output — a per-run artifact, not source. It quotes failure
# messages verbatim, so tracking it makes the gate trip on its own output.
tracking/RELEASE_GATE_RESULT.json

# Pytest junit reports are per-run artifacts wherever they land, so they are
# ignored at any depth. A junit.xml that is a committed test FIXTURE is a
# deliverable, not an artifact, and is re-included below. On 2026-10-10 P060
# lost its required fixture to a bare junit.xml in its own .gitignore, which
# matched at every depth. The per-product patterns are now anchored to the
# product root and this block is the repo-wide guard. Each case below was
# verified with git check-ignore -v on 2026-10-11.
**/junit.xml
**/junit_self.xml
!products/*/fixtures/**/junit.xml
